WEBVTT

00:04.650 --> 00:06.887
Your first training right is the simplest.

00:06.887 --> 00:09.125
You get trained before you're sent to work.

00:09.125 --> 00:12.388
For a new underground miner, Part 48 requires at

00:12.388 --> 00:14.775
least forty hours, with about eight of them at

00:14.775 --> 00:17.613
the mine site. For a new surface miner,

00:17.613 --> 00:20.138
it's at least twenty-four hours, and at least eight

00:20.138 --> 00:22.825
of those must come before you're assigned to work.

00:23.953 --> 00:25.565
That's why you're in this course.

00:26.862 --> 00:29.687
MSHA's guide says miners have a right to receive

00:29.687 --> 00:32.425
required training during normal working hours,

00:32.425 --> 00:34.550
and to be paid for that time at their regular rate

00:34.550 --> 00:37.162
of pay, if they work for the operator.

00:37.162 --> 00:39.262
If the training is somewhere other than your normal

00:39.262 --> 00:42.325
workplace, you must be compensated for added costs

00:42.325 --> 00:45.200
such as mileage, meals, and lodging.

00:46.333 --> 00:48.620
You also have the right to withdraw from the mine

00:48.620 --> 00:50.783
if you haven't had the required training.

00:50.783 --> 00:53.533
You can't be fired, discriminated against,

00:53.533 --> 00:56.858
or lose pay for doing that. And if MSHA withdraws

00:56.858 --> 00:59.170
you because you lack training, you're entitled

00:59.170 --> 01:01.995
to pay from then until you've received the training

01:01.995 --> 01:04.045
and the inspector has verified it.

01:07.391 --> 01:10.303
Part 48 also requires task training.

01:10.303 --> 01:13.391
For certain tasks, like operating mobile equipment,

01:13.391 --> 01:16.316
drilling, working around haulage and conveyors,

01:16.316 --> 01:19.066
running ground-control machines, or blasting,

01:19.066 --> 01:21.603
you must be trained on the task before you do it.

01:21.603 --> 01:23.678
If you're ever asked to do one of those jobs and

01:23.678 --> 01:26.566
nobody has shown you, say so and ask.

01:26.566 --> 01:29.103
Your site's training plan lists what applies.

01:30.220 --> 01:33.833
Every year, every miner gets annual refresher training,

01:33.833 --> 01:37.133
at least eight hours, covering topics like standards,

01:37.133 --> 01:40.883
communication systems, first aid, electrical hazards,

01:40.883 --> 01:43.470
and prevention of accidents. At Allen,

01:43.470 --> 01:46.358
you'll hear it called A R T, for annual refresher

01:46.358 --> 01:47.133
training.

01:48.275 --> 01:51.412
Part 48 training has to be taught by an MSHA-approved

01:51.412 --> 01:55.137
instructor, under a training plan that MSHA approves.

01:55.137 --> 01:57.550
You have a right to see it. Before the plan goes

01:57.550 --> 02:00.675
to MSHA for approval, the operator must post it

02:00.675 --> 02:03.687
on the bulletin board or give each miner a copy,

02:03.687 --> 02:06.587
at least two weeks ahead. If you have comments,

02:06.587 --> 02:09.025
you can submit them in writing, to the operator

02:09.025 --> 02:10.912
or directly to MSHA.

02:12.040 --> 02:14.702
If you've worked at a mine before and come back,

02:14.702 --> 02:17.102
the rules depend on how long you've been gone.

02:17.102 --> 02:19.765
If you were away twelve months or less and return

02:19.765 --> 02:22.265
to the same mine, you must be trained on major

02:22.265 --> 02:24.852
changes that could affect your health and safety.

02:24.852 --> 02:27.053
If you were away more than twelve months,

02:27.053 --> 02:28.490
you must be retrained.

02:31.815 --> 02:35.190
When you complete each MSHA-approved training program,

02:35.190 --> 02:38.527
your operator has to record and certify it on MSHA

02:38.527 --> 02:42.477
Form 5000-23. A copy goes to you when the training

02:42.477 --> 02:45.527
is done. The training certificates for every miner

02:45.527 --> 02:48.815
must be kept at the mine site, where MSHA,

02:48.815 --> 02:51.177
the miners, a miners' representative,

02:51.177 --> 02:53.402
and state inspectors can examine them.

02:53.402 --> 02:55.690
When you leave an employer, you're entitled to

02:55.690 --> 02:58.677
a copy of your certificates. And the operator keeps

02:58.677 --> 03:01.940
copies for currently employed miners for two years,

03:01.940 --> 03:04.440
or for sixty days after employment ends.

03:05.564 --> 03:07.901
In this course, your instructor signs off that

03:07.901 --> 03:10.802
your 5000-23 is completed.

03:11.931 --> 03:14.831
The certificate has to be true. False certification

03:14.831 --> 03:17.031
that training was given is punishable under the

03:17.031 --> 03:20.131
Mine Act. For you, that means two things.

03:20.131 --> 03:22.531
Check your copy to make sure the courses and the

03:22.531 --> 03:24.956
dates are right. And never sign for training you

03:24.956 --> 03:25.906
didn't get.

03:27.032 --> 03:29.620
Keep your copy somewhere safe, and consider taking

03:29.620 --> 03:32.420
a photo as a backup. If you work for another mine

03:32.420 --> 03:34.932
later, your certificates show what you've already

03:34.932 --> 03:38.257
done. MSHA's guide also says that an experienced

03:38.257 --> 03:40.970
miner returning after more than twelve months away

03:40.970 --> 03:43.895
has to be retrained. So the paper matters.

03:45.026 --> 03:47.039
When you get your certificate, take two minutes

03:47.039 --> 03:49.389
to check it. Is your name spelled right?

03:49.389 --> 03:51.601
Is the mine correct? Are the course,

03:51.601 --> 03:54.251
the date, and the hours right? Does it carry the

03:54.251 --> 03:57.039
required signatures? If anything is off,

03:57.039 --> 03:59.326
tell your instructor right away, while the training

03:59.326 --> 04:02.376
is fresh. It's much easier to fix a mistake now

04:02.376 --> 04:03.714
than a year from now.

04:04.857 --> 04:07.319
To sum up. You're trained before you work,

04:07.319 --> 04:09.894
during working hours, at your regular pay.

04:09.894 --> 04:12.094
You get task training for certain jobs,

04:12.094 --> 04:14.719
and annual refresher training every year.

04:14.719 --> 04:17.944
You get a copy of your Form 5000-23,

04:17.944 --> 04:20.432
and you can examine your record at the mine site.

04:20.432 --> 04:21.994
And if you haven't had the training,

04:21.994 --> 04:24.244
you can withdraw without being punished.

04:25.358 --> 04:28.333
Your site's plans always override this video.
